%[text] %[text:anchor:T_6A95D682] # Nodal Analysis Lab
%[text] [⇦ DC Circuit Analysis Main Menu](file:../MainMenu.m)
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] In this lab, you will perform a nodal analysis of the linear circuit shown below in MATLAB. Afterward, you will build the circuit in Simscape and take voltage measurements to verify your result. Before completing this assignment, consider reviewing [NodalAnalysis.m](<matlab:open(fullfile(currentProject().RootFolder,'Scripts','NodalAnalysis.m'))>).
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![nodal\_labcircuit.png](text:image:188a)
%[text]{"align":"center"} *Circuit to analyze*
%[text] The resistances and sources are
%[text]  $\\begin{array}{l}\nR\_1 = 10 \\ \\Omega\n\\\\\nR\_2 = 1  \\ \\text{k} \\Omega\n\\\\\nR\_3 = 500 \\ \\Omega\n\\\\\nR\_4 = 500 \\ \\Omega\n\\\\\nR\_5 = 20 \\ \\Omega\n\\\\\nR\_6 = 220 \\ \\Omega\n\\\\\nR\_7 = 10 \\ \\Omega\n\\end{array}${"altText":"\begin{array}{l} R\_1 = 10 \ \Omega \\ R\_2 = 1  \ \text{k} \Omega \\ R\_3 = 500 \ \Omega \\ R\_4 = 500 \ \Omega \\ R\_5 = 20 \ \Omega \\ R\_6 = 220 \ \Omega \\ R\_7 = 10 \ \Omega \end{array}"} $\\begin{array}{l}\nI\_{s1} = 100 \\ \\text{mA}\n\\\\\nI\_{s2} = 250 \\ \\text{mA}\n\\end{array}${"altText":"\begin{array}{l} I\_{s1} = 100 \ \text{mA} \\ I\_{s2} = 250 \ \text{mA} \end{array}"}
%[text] Follow the steps below to compute the node voltages at (A), (B), and (C).
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_20A0308B] ### **Part 1. Nodal analysis in MATLAB**
%[text] **Task 1.** Decide which nodes are required to analyze the circuit. Use the indicated ground as the reference node.
%[text] **Task 2.** Apply KCL to each node to generate the equations.
%[text] **Task 3.** Using the equations you derived in **Task 2**, create the matrix form of the equations. 
%[text] **Task 4.** Using the space provided below, define the values of the resistors in ohms and the current sources in amps.
% Define the resistances and current sources

%[text] **Task 5.** With the resistances and voltages defined, you can define the matrix system in MATLAB. Define the coefficient matrix `M` and constant vector `b` in the space below. Then, solve for the vector of node voltages.
% Write your code here

%[text] **Task 6.** If you didn't already compute the voltages at all three points (A, B, and C), do so here.
% Write your code here

%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_7CA594C4] ### **Part 2. Simscape model analysis**
%[text] In this section, you will check your result from **Part 1** by creating a model of the electrical circuit in Simscape and then measuring the currents.
%[text] **Task 7.** Open the model:
%[text]{"align":"center"} [![lab\_model.png](text:image:53c2)](<matlab: NodalAnalysisCircuit>)
%[text]{"align":"center"} [`NodalAnalysisCircuit.slx`](<matlab: NodalAnalysisCircuit>)
%[text] **Task 8.** Complete the model by connecting the circuit elements to match the circuit diagram defined in the previous section.
%[text] **Task 9.** Use the multimeter to measure each of the node voltages.
%[text] **Note:** Watch [this 2-minute instructional video](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/81383420/145589989-f7ae4a32-cab3-405d-b7e8-476e34d697b5.mp4) to learn how to use the virtual multimeter.
